<title>INDIA: India's TELCO jumps 5.0 pct on BSE.</title>
<headline>India's TELCO jumps 5.0 pct on BSE.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Indian truckmaker Tata Engineering &amp; Locomotive Company (TELCO) rose 21.75 rupees, or five percent, to 427 in hectic Friday afternoon trade on the Bombay bourse, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The stock is on fire,&quot; said a trader at a foreign brokerage. &quot;There's good fund-based buying and punters are also covering their position.&quot;</p>
<p>TELCO comes out of a month-long no-delivery period on the Bombay bourse in the current settlement which ends today.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
